<h1>Unweighted Chance Of Winning, or UCOW&#0153; 🐄</h1>

<div class = 'section'>
<p>
<img src = "images/ucow.png" width = "40%" class = 'float-right' />
From the Pointless Data Division of JQMCBP Labs is the Unweighted Chance Of Winning, or UCOW&trade;. 
"UCOW, pronounced at a high-pitched yell 'YOU COW!', stands for Unweighted Chance Of Winning. After the field of teams is whittled down from 64 to 16, the number of remaining bracket permutations drops from, I am not making this up, >9 quintillion (2<sup>63</sup>) to 32,768 (2<sup>15</sup>). UCOW&trade; simulates every one of those 32,768 possible permutations and determines the winner or winners of each permutation. After every permutation is run, results are compiled to show each person (and chimp) just how many of those 32,768 permutations they emerge victorious. I repeat this process twice more, when we are down to 8 teams (2<sup>7</sup> = 128 permutations) and 4 teams (2<sup>3</sup> = 8 permutations). It's very deflating. You're welcome!
</p> 
</p>
</div>

